    {
      "id": "p0090-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The original joke wouldn’t work in a straightforward translation into Japanese, as it plays with the English words “shin” and “shingles”. To compensate, the translator replaced the joke with a similar joke in Japanese that plays with the words kotsu (bone) and tekkotsu (steel frame). The result is a bad Japanese pun on par with the original English pun.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2904305,
          0.3721429,
          0.9110347,
          0.4642857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2904305,
          0.3721429,
          0.9110347,
          0.4642857
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "原笑话利用英文 shin（胫骨）和 shingles（屋顶木瓦）玩双关，直译成日文就不成立了。为此，译者换上了类似的日语笑话，利用 kotsu（骨）与 tekkotsu（钢骨架）的关系。于是，一个和英文原版同样冷的日语双关就诞生了。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
